---
/* ===========================================================================
   COUNTER
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Counts a figure up when it scrolls into view.

   The final value is rendered server-side, so with JavaScript disabled the
   number is simply correct and static. The script in Base.astro only ever
   overwrites it temporarily and always restores the exact original string.

   ACCESSIBILITY: the animating span is hidden from assistive technology and
   a visually hidden copy carries the real value, so a screen reader never
   reads a half-counted number — "twenty-one thousand four hundred and two"
   is worse than useless when the figure is 21,717.

   FORMATS: the script animates every numeric token it finds in the string
   and preserves the surrounding characters, so all of these work unchanged:
       50          21,717 (keeps the comma)      3.4 (keeps one decimal)
       548 × 272   (animates both numbers)       90
   A value of zero is left alone — counting up to nothing is not an effect.
=========================================================================== */
const { value, class: className = '' } = Astro.props;
---

<span class={`counter ${className}`} data-count={value}>
  <span class="counter__display" aria-hidden="true">{value}</span>
  <span class="visually-hidden">{value}</span>
</span>

<style>
  /* Tabular figures so the width does not jitter while digits change. */
  .counter { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
</style>
